# kanshi — output profiles for Niri (arandr + autorandr replacement)
#
# Profiles auto-apply on hotplug and can be switched by name:
#   kanshictl switch <profile>
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Keep machine-specific identifiers out of this file:
# monitor serial numbers, make/model strings, and anything that fingerprints a
# specific desk. Connector names (DP-1, HDMI-A-1) are generic and fine.
#
# Real per-machine profiles — including any "Make Model Serial" matching, which is
# the robust form but leaks hardware identifiers — belong in the include below,
# which is NOT tracked here.
include ~/.config/kanshi/config.d/*

# --- NO GENERIC PROFILES HERE, DELIBERATELY (2026-08-22) ------------------------
# This file used to ship example `docked` and `solo` profiles, with a comment claiming you
# could "override them by defining a same-named profile in config.d/". BOTH HALVES WERE
# WRONG, and together they silently broke multi-monitor switching.
#
# 1. DUPLICATE PROFILE NAMES DO NOT OVERRIDE — kanshi parses both and `kanshictl switch <name>`
#    picks the LATER one, i.e. the generic profile here rather than the machine's real one.
#    Measured on mkDesktop 2026-08-22, from kanshi's own log:
#
#        applying profile 'docked'
#        applying profile output 'HDMI-A-1' on connected head 'HDMI-A-1'
#        applying profile output 'DP-1' on connected head 'DP-1'
#
#    Two outputs matched by CONNECTOR, where that machine's own `docked` matches three by
#    "Make Model Serial". Auto-apply on reload had used the right one, so this failed only on
#    an explicit switch — which is why it looked like an intermittent fault.
#
# 2. THE GEOMETRY OVERLAPPED ANY MODERN PRIMARY. The generic `docked` put a second output at
#    x=1920, which collides with any first output wider than that — 2560 and 3440 panels are
#    the norm across this fleet, so the profile was unusable everywhere it managed to win.
#
# Every machine with an overlay already defines its own `docked` (mkDell, mkMac2014, mkMac2017
# — checked), so nothing here is load-bearing. Real profiles belong in the include above, which
# is NOT tracked: "Make Model Serial" matching is the robust form and leaks hardware serials.
#
# Do NOT reintroduce example profiles under names a machine is likely to use. If you want
# examples, put them in a comment.
#
# Do NOT combine kanshi with nwg-displays: it writes ~/.config/niri/monitor.kdl, and the
# resulting Niri config reload discards every transient change kanshi applied.
